       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for a healthy adult, and it risks serious hepatotoxicity. A single 3,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make that dosing safe.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3000 mg/day total**, which would be a transposition of the daily total and the per-dose amount\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend the original dose, please confirm that and tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still want it checked by pharmacy before I enter it."
      }
